{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788645569173037001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unaware-subwealthy-pintail","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8eaaf7c114ede0ba8ad9597e7c3a239891f2e79ee98e3e463022d763b6efd61e","event_uuid":"8ce02d43-3644-46d7-bbae-9a77e5dfa71b","position":{"commit_sha":"30885316cdb062a2aa516e0cadca2e14ecbb46b7","position":"1788641125855899001-8ce02d43-3644-46d7-bbae-9a77e5dfa71b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"083784353e9449aff780f2e3b203f2823314aeb18e8ea8e0ada518338997aaef","event_uuid":"4a794c67-5ffb-4cf9-9e5b-5f911059c921","position":{"commit_sha":"8c7854456432c3ec1665ee618183d554cd997914","position":"1788641146286165001-4a794c67-5ffb-4cf9-9e5b-5f911059c921"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788641125855899001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4a794c67-5ffb-4cf9-9e5b-5f911059c921","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"00c1-dc03-1f1f-4ffc"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nMeasured, reproducible, and **bounded**: when a bound rebar<->Jira pair loses BOTH its binding-store entry and its `rebar-id:` label, the next reconcile pass creates **one extra rebar ticket and one extra Jira issue**, then converges. It is self-correcting — both new entities are bound and labelled in that same pass, so no further growth occurs — but the duplicate is real, durable, reaches Jira, and needs a human to disposition it.\n\nFound while experimentally excluding the reconciler as the producer of the 08-31/09-01 duplicate burst (`anarchic-princely-raven`, `00c1-dc03-1f1f-4ffc`). It is NOT that incident's cause — that was a local eval harness writing into the live store — but it is a genuine non-zero residual, filed separately so it is not buried inside a finding whose headline is \"excluded\".\n\n## Exact perturbation that produces it\n\nHarness: `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_echo_loop_experiment.py`, test `test_d_outbound_orphan_local_ticket_unbound_and_unlabelled` (real git + real ticket CLI + the stateful Jira fake; no production Jira or store).\n\n1. Start from a locally-authored rebar ticket, bound to its Jira issue, label present.\n2. Delete the binding-store entry AND remove the `rebar-id:<local_id>` label from the Jira issue — the create-then-crash / orphan shape (the applier died between materialising and `binding_store.save()`, which is deferred to end-of-pass at `persist_phase.py:140`).\n3. Run further passes.\n\n## Observed\n\n    local tickets: 2 -> 3   (+1)\n    jira issues  : 2 -> 3   (+1)\n    then stable — later passes issue ZERO writes\n\nTwo independent arms fire in the SAME pass:\n\n- **Inbound adopt** materialises an echo ticket from the now-unmarked issue: `_adopt_stands_down` (`binding_walk.py:375-411`) returns False for an unmarked key, so ADOPT proceeds and mints `jira-<key>`.\n- **Outbound create** mints a second Jira issue: `outbound_differ.py:588` keys create-vs-update solely off the binding store (now empty), and the dedup JQL at `dispatch_one.py:154` (`labels = \"rebar-id:<local_id>\"`) MISSES with the label gone.\n\n## Why it converges\n\nBoth new entities are `bind_confirm`'d and labelled within that same pass, so the next pass takes the update branch at `outbound_differ.py:588` and the adopt arm skips the now-bound key at `binding_walk.py:202`. Growth is +1/+1 exactly once, not per-pass.\n\n## Why the existing guards do not prevent it\n\nEach guard alone is sufficient; this perturbation removes both. Measured in the same harness:\n\n- Label intact, binding gone (perturbation a): dedup JQL hits, **zero growth, zero Jira writes**.\n- Binding intact, label gone (perturbation b): outbound takes the update branch, **total no-op**.\n- Both gone (perturbation d): **+1/+1**.\n\n## Related but distinct\n\n- `injurious-neutral-glowworm` (`21fc-51d7-90ca-4a03`, CLOSED) — DC index lag. Its keyless-pending grace was verified WORKING in this harness: inside the grace window `is_keyless_pending_within_grace` (`dispatch_one.py:148-152`) defers the create and growth is zero. Past the grace one duplicate appears — the acknowledged boundary of a time-boxed grace, not a regression of that fix.\n- `nonmystic-topiary-toadfish` — the dedup JQL this perturbation defeats.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 Decide and RECORD whether +1/+1 on simultaneous loss of both guards is acceptable as-is. \"Bounded and self-correcting, accepted\" is a legitimate answer; it must be a stated decision rather than an omission.\n- [ ] AC2 If not acceptable: add a third identity signal that survives loss of both the binding and the label — e.g. consult the Jira entity property `local_id` (already written by `_inbound_create_writeback_jira` via `set_entity_property`) before taking the outbound create branch.\n- [ ] AC3 Whichever is decided, a test pins the chosen behaviour, driven from the perturbation above.\n\n## Priority rationale\n\np3. A single bounded, self-correcting duplicate per affected pair, requiring simultaneous loss of two independent guards. Not p2: it does not compound and does not grow across passes. Not p4: the duplicate is durable, reaches Jira, and needs manual disposition.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f778-6dd7-8913-4043","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconciler creates one duplicate rebar ticket AND one duplicate Jira issue when a bound pair loses both its binding and its rebar-id label","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8ce02d43-3644-46d7-bbae-9a77e5dfa71b","4a794c67-5ffb-4cf9-9e5b-5f911059c921"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788645569173037001,"uuid":"9e3ae3e2-a9b8-43b1-8c3a-462fd88a7bdd"}